AquaStream360 – Criticality Analysis Section (Page 5)
Complete User Interface and Functional Documentation
________________________________________
1. Section Purpose and Overview
The Criticality Analysis Section is a dedicated analytical workspace designed to perform Failure Mode, Effects, and Criticality Analysis on a water distribution network.
Its primary objective is to allow the user to identify, rank, and evaluate network components whose failure would result in the most severe service degradation.
This analysis enables utilities and engineers to:
•	Prioritize maintenance and rehabilitation
•	Support capital investment planning
•	Improve system resilience and risk awareness
•	Identify single points of failure and structurally critical assets
The section evaluates pipes, pumps, valves, and network segments by temporarily simulating their failure and quantifying the resulting service impact.
________________________________________
2. User Interface Layout and Functional Zones
The interface is organized into three vertical panels, following a logical engineering workflow: Setup → Selection → Results.
2.1 Left Panel – Analysis Setup and Configuration
Defines the type of criticality analysis and the performance criteria used to measure failure impact.
2.2 Center Panel – Component Selection
Provides tools to select and filter the specific network elements included in the analysis.
2.3 Right Panel – Results and Impact Reporting
Displays analysis outcomes and provides visualization and reporting tools.
________________________________________
3. Detailed Description of User Interface Elements
________________________________________
3.1 Left Panel – Analysis Setup Elements
Analysis Mode Buttons
These buttons define the focus and scope of the criticality assessment.
Pipe Criticality
•	Evaluates the impact of individual pipe failures
•	Identifies pipe segments critical to maintaining pressure and connectivity
Pump Criticality
•	Evaluates pumping station failures
•	Assesses changes in hydraulic performance and redundancy
Valve Criticality
•	Evaluates valve failures or misoperations
•	Identifies valves essential for isolation, control, and emergency response
Segment Criticality
•	Evaluates failures of predefined network segments
•	Models the simultaneous failure of all components within a hydraulically isolated zone
•	Represents the most comprehensive and realistic failure scenario
Fire Flow Criticality
•	Specialized analysis combining component failure with firefighting demand
•	Verifies whether fire protection pressure and flow standards are maintained under failure conditions
________________________________________
Explanation for This Section
•	Function: Opens an integrated help panel
•	Provides:
o	Conceptual overview of criticality analysis
o	Definitions of key terms (e.g., Severity, Likelihood, Risk Priority Number)
o	Step-by-step explanation of the workflow
________________________________________
