D.	AquaStream360 – User Feedback & Support Section

Purpose and Access
The Feedback & Support section is dedicated entirely to connecting users with the AquaStream360 development team. It is not part of any analytical workflow. Instead, it provides a direct communication channel for:
•	Reporting bugs
•	Offering suggestions
•	Asking questions
•	Proposing contributions or collaborations
The section also provides links to official social media channels and the AquaStream360 website to keep users connected.
________________________________________
Section Layout Overview
The interface is divided into three main vertical zones:
1. Left Zone – Welcome Message
A visually styled panel presenting a welcome message, explaining the purpose of the section, and encouraging user participation. It thanks users for their support and invites contributions, particularly in areas such as:
•	GIS
•	Data Analysis
•	Artificial Intelligence
•	Hydraulics
2. Center Zone – Feedback Submission Form
This is the primary area for composing and submitting feedback, structured to make your input clear, actionable, and categorized appropriately.
3. Right Zone – Social Media Links
A narrow panel containing buttons that link to AquaStream360’s official social media profiles and website.
________________________________________
Center Zone: Feedback Submission Form – Detailed Guide
The form ensures your feedback is structured and easy to process.
Step 1: Categorize Your Feedback
Select a feedback type before writing your message. This helps the team route your message appropriately. Options include:
•	Report Bugs: Describe issues where the software behaves incorrectly, produces errors, or crashes. Include steps to reproduce the problem.
•	Suggestions: Provide ideas for new features or improvements to existing functionality.
•	Contribution: Express interest in collaborating on development, documentation, translations, or related tasks.
•	Question: Ask a specific question about a feature or the software’s capabilities.
•	Constructive Criticism: Provide detailed feedback on aspects of the software that could be improved from a usability or functionality perspective.
•	Other: General feedback that doesn’t fit the categories above.
Step 2: Write Your Feedback
The form provides two distinct areas for writing your message:
1.	Feedback Title / Summary: A concise, one-line description of your feedback (e.g., “Pump curve editor suggestion” or “Crash when exporting large network”).
2.	Detailed Message Body: The large yellow text box with placeholder text “Type the body only here”. Here you provide full details, including:
•	For Bugs: What you were doing, expected outcome, actual outcome, and any error messages.
•	For Suggestions: Description of the feature, why it is useful, and how it could work.
•	Include as much specific detail as possible to assist the development team.
Step 3: Send Your Feedback
Once complete, submit your feedback using one of the yellow buttons:
•	EMAIL: Sends your feedback directly to the AquaStream360 support team.
•	GITHUB: Opens the project’s GitHub Issues page for formal bug or feature submission.
•	CELL & WHATSAPP: Opens your messaging or WhatsApp application with a pre-filled message or team contact number.
________________________________________
Right Zone: Connect on Social Media
This panel provides quick access to AquaStream360’s official platforms:
•	YouTube
•	Website
•	Twitter
•	Facebook
•	LinkedIn
Clicking a button opens the respective page in your web browser.
________________________________________
How to Use This Section: Workflow
1.	Navigate to the Feedback & Support tab.
2.	Select a Feedback Type: Click the appropriate category button (Report Bugs, Suggestions, etc.).
3.	Compose Your Message:
o	Enter a clear title.
o	Provide detailed information in the large yellow text box.
4.	Send Your Feedback: Choose the preferred sending method (e.g., EMAIL).
5.	(Optional) Follow Updates: Click any social media button to stay connected.


